    ✅ PASS - HTTP 200 (Expected: 200)
  → Step: Cleanup: Restore Default Deployment And Clear Fixture
    ✅ PASS - HTTP 200 (Expected: 200)

▶ Running Scenario: MI-018 — Device Trusts The WFM Server Certificate Via The Root CA (device-mi018-tls-trust)
  Description: MARGO-DEV-MANAGEMENTINTERFACE-018: the client MUST trust the WFM's server certificate through a securely obtained root of trust. Under MIAF this is the trust bundle fetched from MIS (CONFORMANCE_FLOWS_AND_MIAF_MIGRATION.md Part 5.3 Phase 2), not a bespoke /onboarding/certificate call -- mtlsClient() in signing.go already verifies the WFM's SVID chains to that bundle on every single mtls step in this suite, so a successful connection here IS the positive proof. NEGATIVE CASE RETIRED -- the old :3002 untrusted-cert listener isn't mTLS-capable with a real SVID yet; needs its own MIAF-shaped negative fixture, tracked as a follow-up, not silently dropped.
  → Step: Connect To The WFM Over mTLS — Server SVID Verified Against The Trust Bundle
    ✅ PASS - HTTP 200 (Expected: 200)

